@demographics
go-to: menu

**Demographic Groups**

The implemented January 1922 gameplay model uses five main classes whose shares total 100%. The figures are approved design values; historical sourcing remains **TBD — historical research required**.

**Chłopi**: 53% in January 1922. Their share declines linearly to exactly 50% in December 1939.

**Robotnicy**: 27% in January 1922. Their share rises linearly to exactly 30% in December 1939.

**Drobnomieszczaństwo**: approximately 12.22% after normalising the approved opening figures.

**Inteligencja**: approximately 5.56% after normalisation.

**Burżuazja i Ziemiaństwo**: approximately 2.22% after normalisation. It has its own approved opening party-support row.

**Bezrobotni**: starts at 3%. Unemployment is an overlapping economic condition rather than a sixth main class, and retains the existing crisis-era mechanics.

**Mniejszości Narodowe**: 30% of the population and overlapping with the five main classes. The provisional internal composition is approximately 60% Chłopi, 17% Robotnicy, 19% Drobnomieszczaństwo, 3% Inteligencja, and 2% Burżuazja i Ziemiaństwo. These approximate figures do not yet drive a separate intersection calculation. The implemented party-support row is independent; inherited Catholic-targeting PPS effects enter only through a compatibility bridge.


